# warnings

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` is currently lowered to a normal import, because a deferred import evaluates the external module `ext`, and `iife` output gets that module as a global or as a wrapper argument. This changes execution timing because side effects run immediately instead of when the deferred import is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ main.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ import defer * as ns from 'ext';
   │ ────────────────┬───────────────  
   │                 ╰───────────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import.defer()` is currently lowered to `import()`, because a deferred import evaluates the external module `ext`, and `iife` output gets that module as a global or as a wrapper argument. This changes execution timing because the module evaluates when it loads instead of when its namespace is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ main.js:4:27 ]
   │
 4 │ export const load = () => import.defer('ext2');
   │                           ──────────┬─────────  
   │                                     ╰─────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

# Assets

## main.js

```js
var lib = (function(exports, ext) {
	Object.defineProperty(exports, Symbol.toStringTag, { value: "Module" });
	// HIDDEN [\0rolldown/runtime.js]
	ext = __toESM(ext);
	// main.js
	const read = () => ext.value;
	const load = () => import("ext2");
	exports.load = load;
	exports.read = read;
	return exports;
})({}, Ext);

```

